---The SecuritySettings of AzureStackHCI Cluster.
---@class azure.azurestackhci.DeploymentSecuritySettings
---@field hvciProtection? boolean By default, Hypervisor-protected Code Integrity is enabled on your Azure HCI cluster.
---@field drtmProtection? boolean By default, Secure Boot is enabled on your Azure HCI cluster. This setting is hardware dependent.
---@field driftControlEnforced? boolean When set to true, the security baseline is re-applied regularly.
---@field credentialGuardEnforced? boolean When set to true, Credential Guard is enabled.
---@field smbSigningEnforced? boolean When set to true, the SMB default instance requires sign in for the client and server services.
---@field smbClusterEncryption? boolean When set to true, cluster east-west traffic is encrypted.
---@field sideChannelMitigationEnforced? boolean When set to true, all the side channel mitigations are enabled
---@field bitlockerBootVolume? boolean When set to true, BitLocker XTS_AES 256-bit encryption is enabled for all data-at-rest on the OS volume of your Azure Stack HCI cluster. This setting is TPM-hardware dependent.
---@field bitlockerDataVolumes? boolean When set to true, BitLocker XTS-AES 256-bit encryption is enabled for all data-at-rest on your Azure Stack HCI cluster shared volumes.
---@field wdacEnforced? boolean WDAC is enabled by default and limits the applications and the code that you can run on your Azure Stack HCI cluster.

